                <head>200. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>A memorandum for the Special Group charged with responsibility for fostering
                    insurrection in Cuba (Operation Mongoose), May 31, 1962, noted that at its
                    meeting on March 22, Attorney General Robert Kennedy had asked “what would be an
                    appropriate course of action for the United States to take in the event that the
                    Soviets establish a military base in Cuba.” The memorandum noted the Department
                    of Defenseʼs concern over the issue and proposed that each participating agency
                    prepare a written response to Kennedyʼs question. For text of the memorandum,
                    see <ref target="frus:frus1961-63v10/pg_824"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations,</hi> 1961–1963 volume X, page 824</ref>.</p>
            </div>
